  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:credential-verification",
  "domain": "security",
  "definition": "Credential verification is the process of cryptographically or institutionally confirming the authenticity, integrity, and validity of a credential \u2014 such as a digital certificate, verifiable credential, or identity assertion \u2014 issued by a trusted authority to a subject, so that a relying party can grant access or trust without contacting the original issuer. In decentralised identity systems it relies on public-key cryptography and distributed ledgers to enable privacy-preserving, tamper-evident verification. The process must also check revocation status to ensure credentials that have been invalidated cannot be fraudulently reused.",
